      "title": "README - StoryTeller FastH3",
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Geekatplay StoryTeller - MiniMax FastH3\n**Geekatplay Studio - Vladimir Chopine**\nhttps://www.geekatplay.com\n\n### How to run\n1. **Story Director** - type a premise, pick style / aspect / mood, set how many segments.\n   Ollama is optional: if `http://127.0.0.1:11434` is unreachable the node falls back to its\n   built-in procedural director, so the queue never fails. The model dropdown lists what is\n   already on your Ollama first; `qwen3:8b` is pulled automatically on first use if missing.\n2. **Story Batch Renderer** - renders every segment with FastH3 in 8 steps, checkpoints each\n   one to disk, trims the seam frame and mixes audio.\n3. **SaveVideo** - writes the finished movie.\n\n### Required models\n| Slot | File |\n|---|---|\n| diffusion_models | `fastvideo_fasth3_8step_v2_pruned_int8_convrot.safetensors` |\n| text_encoders | `qwen3vl_32b_minimax_h3_nvfp4_awq.safetensors` |\n| vae | `minimax_h3_video_vae_fp16.safetensors` |\n| vae (audio) | `minimax_h3_audio_vae_fp32.safetensors` |\n\n### Sampler settings\n`steps 8`, `euler`, `simple`, `shift_video 10.0`, `shift_audio 3.0` - these match the\nreference FastH3 workflow. The shifts are **not** optional: FastH3 will not converge without them.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        -1420,
